# Keep build output out of the image context.
#
# There was no .dockerignore anywhere, so every image build shipped this whole service directory —
# including obj/ and bin/, roughly 100 MB per service and 1.1 GB across the repo. Two costs: the
# context is uploaded to the daemon on every build, and a stale artifact sitting in bin/ can be copied
# into the image ahead of the fresh compile that was supposed to replace it.
#
# NOTE: .dockerignore is resolved against the BUILD CONTEXT, not the repo root. These builds set
# context to this service directory, so the file has to live here — one at the repo root has no effect
# at all. That is why there are sixteen of these; scripts/ci/validate_dockerignore.py asserts they stay
# identical. See #241.
**/obj/
**/bin/
**/.vs/
**/*.user
**/*.lscache
**/*.DS_Store

# Tests never ship. The image builds src/ only.
tests/

# Local editor and tooling noise
.idea/
.vscode/
